From: freeforall1932-design <300004558+freeforall1932-design@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 04 Oct 2026 09:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] P1-37 / U-57: wasm page must never read a stale
 /out.gif — clear + verify around callMain

Finding U-57 (E:NA-05, fix-order P1-37, state OPEN at main fe4f0a7):

    WASM singleton reuses stale /out.gif — wasm.js does not unlink/snapshot
    /out.gif before callMain(); after one success, an exit-zero/no-write run
    reads the previous GIF and reports success for the wrong input.

The Emscripten module is created once (lazy singleton, one module for many
runs), so its virtual FS survives from run to run. The page wrote /in.gif,
called callMain(), and read /out.gif unconditionally — the exact
false-success shape the desktop closed with U-59 snapshots and the CLI with
the N-15 partial snapshot.

Fix, desktop-parity honest:

  * new web/wasm/fs_run_guard.mjs — pure ESM, no DOM, no Emscripten import
    (Node runs it directly; that is how the suite below proves it):
      - clearRunArtifacts(FS, paths): unlink /in.gif and /out.gif BEFORE the
        run; anything readable afterwards was written by THIS callMain.
      - readVerifiedGif(FS, path): the read-back admission rule — exists,
        non-empty, GIF87a/GIF89a magic (the server's U-92 gate, same bar).
  * wasm.js calls the guard around the engine call and keeps the original
    two status messages verbatim ("...no output..." / "...not a GIF..."),
    so no UI wording drifts.

Proof (failing-first leg included):

  web/test/u57-stale-output.test.mjs (plain node, zero deps):
    T1  RED leg — replays the ORIGINAL sequence against a fake MEMFS and
        asserts the audit's claim is real: without clearing, run 2
        (exit 0, writes nothing) reports the run-1 GIF — the bug, caught.
    T2  the FIXED sequence refuses that run with reason "missing".
    T3  clearRunArtifacts removes both fixed paths and is idempotent.
    T4  readVerifiedGif admission table: missing/empty/not-gif/GIF87a/GIF89a.
    T5  three consecutive real runs each return their own product bytes.

Ship note: the wasm track stays NOT SHIPPABLE (OD-16 / N-32) — this patch
closes a correctness finding so the track stops lying, it does not promote
it. Register bookkeeping after green proof: §5 row U-57 -> FIXED with the
node output, check_docs.sh --emit, re-anchor the G10 base line.
